(16, 'Cookies', '<section class=\"section\"><div class=\"container\"><div class=\"content-detail\"><h3 class=\"color-brand-2\">EU Cookie Consent</h3><p class=\"font-md color-grey-900\">To use this website we are using Cookies and collecting some Data. To be compliant with the EU GDPR we give you to choose if you allow us to use certain Cookies and to collect some Data. .</p><p>There are two primary modes of sea freight transportation: Full Container Load (FCL) and Less than Container Load (LCL). FCL is used when the shipment is large enough to fill an entire container. On the other hand, LCL is used when the shipment does not require a full container. In this case, the goods are combined with other shipments to fill a container. Both modes have their advantages and disadvantages.</p><p>There are two primary modes of sea freight transportation: Full Container Load (FCL) and Less than Container Load (LCL). FCL is used when the shipment is large enough to fill an entire container. On the other hand, LCL is used when the shipment does not require a full container. In this case, the goods are combined with other shipments to fill a container. Both modes have their advantages and disadvantages.</p><h3>Essential Data</h3><div class=\"row align-items-center\"><div class=\"col-lg-12\"><p>The Essential Data is needed to run the Site you are visiting technically. You can not deactivate them.</p><p>Session Cookie: PHP uses a Cookie to identify user sessions. Without this Cookie the Website is not working.</p><p>XSRF-Token Cookie: Laravel automatically generates a CSRF \"token\" for each active user session managed by the application. This token is used to verify that the authenticated user is the one actually making the requests to the application.</p></div></div></div></div></section>', 1, NULL, 'default', '', 'draft', '2025-01-17 18:19:32', '2025-02-14 14:48:14'),
(17, 'Terms of service', '<h1 data-start=\"219\" data-end=\"255\"><strong data-start=\"221\" data-end=\"255\">Workshop IT - Terms of Service</strong></h1><h2 data-start=\"257\" data-end=\"281\"><strong data-start=\"260\" data-end=\"279\">1. Introduction</strong></h2><p data-start=\"282\" data-end=\"705\">Welcome to <strong data-start=\"293\" data-end=\"308\">Workshop IT</strong>! These Terms of Service (\"Terms\") govern your access to and use of our services, including but not limited to training, consulting, web development, cybersecurity services, and other IT-related solutions provided by Workshop IT (\"we,\" \"our,\" or \"us\"). By using our services, you agree to comply with and be bound by these Terms. If you do not agree with these Terms, you may not use our services.</p><hr><h2 data-start=\"712\" data-end=\"741\"><strong data-start=\"715\" data-end=\"739\">2. Services Overview</strong></h2><p data-start=\"742\" data-end=\"799\">Workshop IT provides a range of IT services, including:</p><ul data-start=\"800\" data-end=\"958\"><li data-start=\"800\" data-end=\"829\">IT Training and Workshops</li><li data-start=\"830\" data-end=\"858\">Cybersecurity Consulting</li><li data-start=\"859\" data-end=\"889\">Web Development and Design</li><li data-start=\"890\" data-end=\"927\">Technical Support and Maintenance</li><li data-start=\"928\" data-end=\"958\">Digital Business Solutions</li></ul><p data-start=\"960\" data-end=\"1036\">Our services may be updated or modified from time to time at our discretion.</p><hr><h2 data-start=\"1043\" data-end=\"1076\"><strong data-start=\"1046\" data-end=\"1074\">3. User Responsibilities</strong></h2><p data-start=\"1077\" data-end=\"1115\">By using our services, you agree to:</p><ul data-start=\"1116\" data-end=\"1424\"><li data-start=\"1116\" data-end=\"1214\">Provide accurate and up-to-date information when registering or interacting with our services.</li><li data-start=\"1215\" data-end=\"1261\">Use our services for lawful purposes only.</li><li data-start=\"1262\" data-end=\"1338\">Respect the intellectual property rights of Workshop IT and other users.</li><li data-start=\"1339\" data-end=\"1424\">Not engage in activities that could harm or disrupt our services or infrastructure.</li></ul><hr><h2 data-start=\"1431\" data-end=\"1459\"><strong data-start=\"1434\" data-end=\"1457\">4. Payment and Fees</strong></h2><ul data-start=\"1460\" data-end=\"1708\"><li data-start=\"1460\" data-end=\"1550\">All fees for services are detailed on our website or agreed upon in written contracts.</li><li data-start=\"1551\" data-end=\"1641\">Payments must be made as per the terms specified in your service agreement or invoice.</li><li data-start=\"1642\" data-end=\"1708\">Late payments may result in service suspension or termination.</li></ul><hr><h2 data-start=\"1715\" data-end=\"1757\"><strong data-start=\"1718\" data-end=\"1755\">5. Cancellation and Refund Policy</strong></h2><ul data-start=\"1758\" data-end=\"2033\"><li data-start=\"1758\" data-end=\"1855\">You may cancel your subscription or service contract at any time by providing written notice.</li><li data-start=\"1856\" data-end=\"2033\">Refunds will be issued according to the terms specified in your service agreement. For training services, refunds may not be available once a workshop or course has started.</li></ul><hr><h2 data-start=\"2040\" data-end=\"2073\"><strong data-start=\"2043\" data-end=\"2071\">6. Intellectual Property</strong></h2><ul data-start=\"2074\" data-end=\"2302\"><li data-start=\"2074\" data-end=\"2208\">All content, materials, and tools provided by Workshop IT are the intellectual property of Workshop IT unless otherwise specified.</li><li data-start=\"2209\" data-end=\"2302\">You may not reproduce, distribute, or modify our materials without prior written consent.</li></ul><hr><h2 data-start=\"2309\" data-end=\"2344\"><strong data-start=\"2312\" data-end=\"2342\">7. Limitation of Liability</strong></h2><p data-start=\"2345\" data-end=\"2377\">Workshop IT is not liable for:</p><ul data-start=\"2378\" data-end=\"2631\"><li data-start=\"2378\" data-end=\"2480\">Any direct, indirect, incidental, or consequential damages resulting from the use of our services.</li><li data-start=\"2481\" data-end=\"2545\">Loss of data, business interruption, or any system failures.</li><li data-start=\"2546\" data-end=\"2631\">Issues arising from third-party services or integrations used with our solutions.</li></ul><hr><h2 data-start=\"2638\" data-end=\"2664\"><strong data-start=\"2641\" data-end=\"2662\">8. Privacy Policy</strong></h2><p data-start=\"2665\" data-end=\"2799\">Your privacy is important to us. Please review our <strong data-start=\"2716\" data-end=\"2734\">Privacy Policy</strong> to understand how we collect, use, and protect your information.</p><hr><h2 data-start=\"2806\" data-end=\"2855\"><strong data-start=\"2809\" data-end=\"2853\">9. Service Modifications and Termination</strong></h2><ul data-start=\"2856\" data-end=\"3077\"><li data-start=\"2856\" data-end=\"2958\">Workshop IT reserves the right to modify or discontinue services at any time without prior notice.</li><li data-start=\"2959\" data-end=\"3077\">We may terminate or suspend your access to services if you violate these Terms or engage in prohibited activities.</li></ul><hr><h2 data-start=\"3084\" data-end=\"3110\"><strong data-start=\"3087\" data-end=\"3108\">10. Governing Law</strong></h2><p data-start=\"3111\" data-end=\"3225\">These Terms shall be governed by and interpreted in accordance with the laws of [Your Jurisdiction/State/Country].</p><hr><h2 data-start=\"3232\" data-end=\"3265\"><strong data-start=\"3235\" data-end=\"3263\">11. Changes to the Terms</strong></h2><p data-start=\"3266\" data-end=\"3437\">We may update these Terms from time to time. Any changes will be posted on our website, and your continued use of our services constitutes acceptance of the updated Terms.</p><hr><h2 data-start=\"3444\" data-end=\"3467\"><strong data-start=\"3447\" data-end=\"3465\">12. Contact Us</strong></h2><p data-start=\"3468\" data-end=\"3646\">If you have any questions about these Terms, please contact us:<br><strong data-start=\"3534\" data-end=\"3549\">Workshop IT</strong><br>Email: [Insert Email Address]<br>Phone: [Insert Phone Number]<br>Website: [Insert Website URL]</p>', 1, NULL, 'default', '', 'published', '2025-01-17 18:19:32', '2025-02-14 15:03:20'),
(18, 'Privacy Policy', '<section class=\"section\">\n    <div class=\"container\">\n        <div class=\"content-detail\">\n            <h3 class=\"color-brand-2\">EU Cookie Consent</h3>\n            <p class=\"font-md color-grey-900\">To use this website we are using Cookies and collecting some Data. To be compliant with the EU GDPR we give you to choose if you allow us to use certain Cookies and to collect some Data. .</p>\n            <p>There are two primary modes of sea freight transportation: Full Container Load (FCL) and Less than Container Load (LCL). FCL is used when the shipment is large enough to fill an entire container. On the other hand, LCL is used when the shipment does not require a full container. In this case, the goods are combined with other shipments to fill a container. Both modes have their advantages and disadvantages.</p>\n            <p>There are two primary modes of sea freight transportation: Full Container Load (FCL) and Less than Container Load (LCL). FCL is used when the shipment is large enough to fill an entire container. On the other hand, LCL is used when the shipment does not require a full container. In this case, the goods are combined with other shipments to fill a container. Both modes have their advantages and disadvantages.</p>\n            <h3>Essential Data</h3>\n            <div class=\"row align-items-center\">\n                <div class=\"col-lg-12\">\n                    <p>The Essential Data is needed to run the Site you are visiting technically. You can not deactivate them.</p>\n                    <p>Session Cookie: PHP uses a Cookie to identify user sessions. Without this Cookie the Website is not working.</p>\n                    <p>XSRF-Token Cookie: Laravel automatically generates a CSRF \"token\" for each active user session managed by the application. This token is used to verify that the authenticated user is the one actually making the requests to the application.</p>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n</section>\n', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', '2025-01-17 18:19:32', '2025-01-17 18:19:32'),
